Data license: TBD -- placeholder, must be resolved before making the repo public.

This benchmark combines three sources with different provenance:

1. `synthetic` records: generated by us (Week 2). No third-party rights
   issue; fine to license permissively (e.g. CC-BY-4.0) once decided.
2. `longmemeval` records: extracted from the LongMemEval benchmark. Check
   LongMemEval's own license before deciding how (or whether) to
   redistribute derived text.
3. `locomo` records: extracted from the LoCoMo benchmark. Check LoCoMo's
   own license before deciding how (or whether) to redistribute derived
   text.

Until this is resolved: `data/raw/` and `data/processed/` (which contain
the full text) are gitignored and NOT part of this repository's public
git history. Only `data/samples/` (60 records) and `data/splits/*_ids.txt`
are committed -- if either upstream license turns out to be restrictive,
review `data/samples/memories_sample.jsonl` specifically before the repo
goes public, since it does contain real longmemeval/locomo-derived text.
